A||N||2||jlruiz67||Tune up.........what do you change??||||5||
Z||000000||jlruiz67||04-19-2001||03:48 PM||||Hello all, I did a search and didn't find much on the subject. I want to do a major tune up and like to know from the smallest item to the big, what do you replace or inspect when doing a major and minor tune up.<P>I hope this can help many of us, to get a complete list of items to check, inspect or replace<P>Thank you all||||reg||5
Z||000001||AkursedX||04-19-2001||04:06 PM||||Hmm, well I'll try to make this list as full as I can:<P>Check/replace<BR>Oil<BR>Spark Plugs/wires<BR>Distributor cap and rotor<BR>Fuel Filter<BR>Air filter<BR>Lube up ball joints and tierod ends<BR>Inspect brakes/parking brake<BR>Change oil<BR>Inspect vacuum lines for cracks<P>And that's about all i can think of, hope this helps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||04-19-2001||10:40 PM||||Also:<BR>Pick-up coil/module (the guts of the distributor, especially if it hasn't been done before!)<BR>O2 sensor (I think its supposed to be changed out every 30 K but I do mine every other year)<P>Things to check out are: <BR>fan belts<BR>tranny fluid level (hey, better to find out now about a leaky tranny seal or pan gasket!)<BR>Coolant hoses<P>Maybe give a squirt of cleaner to: <BR>PCV valve (on the valve cover)  <BR>idle air control valve (on the the throttle body.)<P>Remember the whole idea of a tune up is preventative maintenance. Not allowing things that would strand you on the side of the road to wear out! Once you add this all up it could get pretty expensive but hey, you wanted to know! Some people get even more intense even changing out their brake and clutch fluid!||||reg||6
